PRE-TABLE AMENDMENT, PASS 10 -- its own file (mtime against part10/driver.log is the order witness).

SECTION 18 -- the CLASS CLOSURE of the joint cells at TxICR, under the rule pass 10 adopted.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* THE RULE (fable5, the rule-question seat; codex independently in equivalence-class form; now CLAUDE.md
  clause (d), JOINT CELLS): a joint cell is in the closure exactly when the guarded body's OWN CODE
  distinguishes it -- each lvalue at the partition the body's own tests induce; the enumerated cells
  are the CROSS-PRODUCT of those partitions, never arbitrary boolean functions of the read-set.
* THE DENOMINATOR, read off dev_pcc2.c:515-543 (the TxICR write body's own `if's): SEVEN partitions --
  the label (== T1ICR / T2ICR), idata & IEN, idata & ICLR, the register's INT bit, pending1 > 0,
  pending2 > 0, idata & 0xe0 -- 128 cells.  The pass-9 repair rowed ONE cell of the (label, p1, p2)
  product and pass 10 found two of its neighbours open (M_T1JOINT, M_P2T1: both predicted 194/194 by
  the Opus seat before its build; M_P2T1 also by codex from reading).
* ROWED HERE, all sixteen cells of {label} x {p1} x {p2} x {idata & IEN}: three EXISTING sessions each
  wide-write at BOTH labels with idata 0x0000 and 0x0013 (IEN|IL3 -- so a landed write reads 0x33 or
  0x13, never the preset; the part-6 lesson), the idle timer's ICR preset to 0x11 first; the decl rows
  stay at 1 (the announce is latched once per block -- hand-verified DECL=1 with four declines); nine
  new readbacks.  No new session, no new load sensitivity.  The (label, 0, 0, *)
  cells are the plain rows (`latch all' drives 3 = IEN clear; `rb t*icr' 0xaab8 = IEN set).
* NOT ROWED, DISCLOSED WITH THE COUNT: the ICLR, INT and 0xe0 partitions (112 cells).  They govern what
  a landed write DOES to the counts (the ICLR decrement and INT clear, the HUH? print), not whether it
  lands; rowing them costs about thirty more wide writes.  PASS 11 IS ASKED whether the adopted rule
  demands them -- stated here rather than argued, because the alternative is a pass-12 finding of
  exactly that shape.
* Records folded in (grok, codex, Opus): `>= 8' where the masked ovfhi rows are described; the BIT
  COVERAGE set marks 0x81 as masked; bit 3 is inside the store mask but no row holds it SET; the
  guest-ordinary-state warrant is COC on BOTH timers (both-thousands, disclosed: the body tests > 0
  only); `pendboth arm1' observes a STICKY INT bit; the pass-9 heading's roster arithmetic;
  'load-STABLE' narrowed to value-stable-after-the-callback.
* The `||' form and the single-count forms were killed by pre-existing rows (grok, codex, Opus by
  derivation); not re-measured.
* Opus (pass 10) on the record, folded in: the guest-state premise (OpenBSD clock + statclock) is
  NOT checkable in this tree -- no OpenBSD source, no PCC2 datasheet among the fifteen PDFs -- and
  grok's clock.c reading is recorded as unverified; the in-tree warrant is the model's own joint
  handling (one callback services both timers; reassert reads both counts).  `pendboth arm1' now
  says the proof of both-non-zero is the MUTANT reddening the rows, not the sticky INT readback.
  The masked ovfhi rows' kill channel is CEN alone (bit 7 is arming; bits 1-6 pinned only by ovf*),
  so their driven value must keep bit 0 clear -- stated in the contract.  Opus predicted `pendboth
  decl' would become 2 with a second wide write; the announce is LATCHED once per block and the
  hand-verification measured 1, which is why the decl rows stay at 1.
* HAND-VERIFIED before writing, on the restored part-9 clone (`p11_try.py'): pend2 0x31 0x31 0x31 0x11 0x11,
  pend1 the same, pendboth 0x31 x6, DECL=1 each -- which is how the latched announce was found before
  the table rather than by it.
THE FOUR MANDATED CHECKS (run, not asserted; Opus pass 10 found PRETABLE_pass9.out carried none):
* SIBLING PARITY -- at a SHARED block the siblings are the LABELS (the clause this pass adds): the
  T1/T2 census over the 194 names showed every operator-reachable TxICR/TxCTL cell since pass 6
  doubled at T1 EXCEPT pendboth (Opus).  After this diff every timer session writes at both labels;
  the guest path (hrd/hwr/acc/brd2/rb2) stays T2-only by construction and is disclosed as such.
* CLAIM -> ROW -- new contract sentences: "every one held at a wide write" (sixteen cells) -> the nine
  new readbacks plus the seven existing ones named cell by cell; "a landed write reads 0x33 / 0x13 /
  0x00, never the preset" -> the presets 0x11 and the values 0x0000 / 0x0013 in the rows; "the announce
  is latched once per block" -> the decl rows' want of 1 with the hand-verified DECL=1; "the ICLR, INT
  and 0xe0 partitions are not rowed" -> no row, disclosed by count (an owed SENTENCE, written).
* GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD -- the guard reads len and writeflag; the body reads reg[relative_addr],
  idata, relative_addr, pending1, pending2.  The disagreeing states are exactly the cells: the guard
  cannot see the counts or the label, so a guard conditioned on them declines or lands with no channel
  of its own -- the readbacks are the channel, and every cell has one.
* CHANNEL -- per new row, the mutant it kills and the observable that differs: pend2 rbi <- M_P2IEN
  (0x33 vs 0x31); pend2 rb1 <- M_P2T1 (0x00 vs 0x11); pend2 rb1i <- M_P2T1 / M_P2IEN (0x13 vs 0x11);
  pend1 rbi <- (no enumerated mutant: the (T1, >0, 0, IEN) cell, held for completeness, disclosed as
  unkilled); pend1 rb2 / rb2i <- M_P1XT2 (0x00 / 0x13 vs 0x11); pendboth rbi <- M_P2IEN (0x33 vs
  0x31); pendboth rb1 <- M_T1JOINT / M_P2T1 (0x20 vs 0x31); pendboth rb1i <- M_T1JOINT (0x20) /
  M_P2T1 (0x33) / M_P2IEN (0x13) vs 0x31.  One row, pend1 rbi, has no mutant in this table -- said
  here rather than left to be found.
PREDICTIONS for part 10 (five mutants plus BASE, 203-row instrument):
    BASE            203/203
    (derived from the body: a LANDED IEN-clear write zeroes that timer's count, so a count-conditioned
     guard RE-ARMS for the session's later writes; the announce is latched once per block, so a decl
     row reds only when the session's FIRST wide write lands)
    M_PENDBOTH      200/203   pendboth decl (0: the first write landed), rb (0x20), rbi (0x20: declined after p2 was zeroed);
                              rb1 / rb1i green (0x31: guard re-armed)
    M_T1JOINT       201/203   pendboth rb1 (0x20), rb1i (0x20: declined after p1 was zeroed); decl 1, rb/rbi green
    M_P2T1          199/203   pendboth rb1 (0x20), rb1i (0x33: p2 untouched, the second T1 write lands too); pend2 rb1 (0x00), rb1i (0x13); decls 1; pendn2 green
    M_P1XT2         201/203   pend1 rb2 (0x00), rb2i (0x13); decl 1; pendboth and pendn1 green
    M_P2IEN         199/203   pend2 rbi (0x33), rb1i (0x13); pendboth rbi (0x33), rb1i (0x13); decls 1 (the IEN-clear first writes are declined); pendn2 green
